    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Imbrăsus</span></b> , i,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				companion of Æneas</i>, <i>father of
				Glaucus and Lades</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				12, 343</span></i>.—The latter called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Imbrăsĭdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>acc. plur.</i>
			Imbrasidas, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 12, 343</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Asius Imbrasides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 123</span></i>
			.</div>
